{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>There is something</b>. The word יש is found in most cases in the sacred language for that which exists; occasionally for that which occurs at times, as in ויש אשר יהיה הענן (Ecclesiastes 11:3), יש מפזר ונוסף (Ecclesiastes 5:12), ויש רשע מאריך (Ecclesiastes 8:12) — for when the years of the wicked are many, [their days] are cut short. And if something new appears to a person, it already existed in עולמים. The meaning of עולמים is like זמנים, as in צור עולמים (Isaiah 26:4), מלכות כל עולמים (Psalms 103:19 — 'his kingdom is a kingdom of all עולמים'), תשועת עולמים (Isaiah 45:17) — eternal salvation and many times."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:26:48.493772785Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}